{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_9c7314046713679d29d4c044cb4a452793a3f40505ce800babbef04e7ea54384", "title": "Diary of a Chav", "text": "Diary of a Chav is a young adult series that was written by the English journalist, author, and broadcaster Grace Dent. The series consists of six books that were originally released in the United Kingdom from 2007 to 2009. An attempt to publish the books overseas in the United States was largely unsuccessful and only the first two books, re-titled for American publication, were released.", "score": 28.1767}, {"id": "hp_doc_53dc2b703c065f6acad0904c36210893e9bb1f344333fc79a962a28afa53d958", "title": "The Diary of a Young Girl", "text": "The Diary of a Young Girl, also known as The Diary of Anne Frank, is a book of the writings from the Dutch language diary kept by Anne Frank while she was in hiding for two years with her family during the Nazi occupation of the Netherlands. The family was apprehended in 1944, and Anne Frank died of typhus in the Bergen-Belsen concentration camp in 1945. The diary was retrieved by Miep Gies, who gave it to Anne's father, Otto Frank, the family's only known survivor, just after the war was over. The diary has since been published in more than 60 languages.", "score": 18.2415}, {"id": "hp_doc_38fa845111f8193c1d1b570a4b99dc78e70cd2d864ccc9ba21ee03ba7dbf44e9", "title": "Owen Harris (director)", "text": "He has directed episodes of \"Secret Diary of a Call Girl\", and \"Misfits\", and the TV movies \"Holy Flying Circus\" and \"The Gamechangers\". In 2013, he directed \"Be Right Back\", an episode of the anthology series \"Black Mirror\", and in 2016 he directed a further episode \"San Junipero\".", "score": 14.0892}], "remaining_searches": 2}
